# Scatter Tile Map — MapLibre

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Markers and lines without an access token

Use `Scattermap` with `layout.map`. The MapLibre implementation replaces the
removed Mapbox trace; no access token is needed for `open-street-map` tiles.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scattermap}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(Scattermap.new(
  lat: [40.705, 40.730, 40.758], lon: [-74.013, -73.995, -73.985],
  text: ["Battery Park", "Washington Square", "Times Square"],
  mode: "markers+lines", marker: %{size: 12}, line: %{width: 3}
))
|> Figure.update_layout(
  title: "A route through Manhattan",
  map: %{style: "open-street-map", center: %{lat: 40.73, lon: -74.0}, zoom: 11}
)
|> Plotly.show()
```
